<?xml version="1.0"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSim.xsl"?>
<fdm_config name="CoconutQuadplane" version="2.0" release="BETA"
   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
   xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSim.xsd">

<fileheader>
 <author>Project team; aero data generated with Claude</author>
 <description>
   Fixed-wing CRUISE-PHASE model. VTOL lift/transition stays with ArduPilot's
   built-in SITL QuadPlane model; JSBSim's job here is higher-fidelity
   fixed-wing aerodynamics for the cruise/survey segment.

   AERO DATA IS REAL (no longer placeholder):
   - 2D sections: SD7037 (wing) and NACA 0009 (tail) through NeuralFoil
     (an XFOIL surrogate) at cruise Reynolds number (~1.9e5, V = 12 m/s,
     MAC = 236 mm), n_crit = 7 for a matte foam surface.
   - 3D coefficients: AeroSandbox AeroBuildup component build-up over the real
     planform (wing + H-tail + twin fins + 46 cm pod + 4 booms), cross-checked
     against AeroSandbox VLM and a Munk slender-body fuselage yaw estimate.
     See aero/RESULTS.md and aero/coefficients.json.
   - Longitudinal C_L is tabulated so the stall knee shows; C_D and C_m carry
     the real derivatives. Lateral-directional axes are populated (6-DOF).

   DESIGN POINT baked in (refined from the earlier decision memo):
   - wing incidence 1.0 deg  (2 deg gave negative trim alpha for this light
     wing loading), cruise 12 m/s, AUW 1.4 kg, CG 33% MAC (static margin ~27%).
   - tail incidence -1.79 deg vs fuselage (-2.79 vs wing chord) trims cruise.
   - VERTICAL FINS ENLARGED to 340 cm2 total (170 cm2 each, V_V ~ 0.044): the
     old 210 cm2 gave C_n_beta ~ 0.02, short of the 0.07 target for a
     rudderless UAV. Metrics + C_n_beta below reflect the enlarged fin.
   - Wing dihedral ~3 deg is assumed for C_l_beta (add it to the build).
   - Control derivatives (Cmde, CLde, Clda) are from aero/control_authority.py
     (full-span 28%c elevons). Authority is abundant, not marginal — expect
     ArduPilot rate/throw limiting. Signs follow JSBSim convention; re-check
     against the elevon mixing at the SITL-bridge step.
   - Forward motor = A2212 2200KV + 1045 (engine/A2212_2200KV.xml + APC_1045),
     replacing the undersized DJI E305 stand-in. See PROPULSION_NOTES.md:
     cruise throttle ~0.34; static NaNs (JSBSim brushless-motor limitation);
     use verify_model.py's power-off checks, not do_simple_trim.
   - SITL BRIDGE additions (see BRIDGE.md): an external_reactions block for
     4 lift rotors + 1 forward + a yaw couple, driven by jsbsim_bridge.py from
     ArduPilot PWM (the propulsion engine is left un-started for the bridge).
     4-point landing gear (the 3-point layout tipped over). alpha/beta are
     clamped to +-25 deg in the derivative terms so a vertical climb does not
     blow up. Elevon de-mix sign verified against ArduPilot fn 77/78.
 </description>
</fileheader>

<metrics>
  <wingarea  unit="M2">   0.300 </wingarea>
  <wingspan  unit="M" >   1.300 </wingspan>
  <wing_incidence unit="DEG"> 1.00 </wing_incidence>
  <chord     unit="M" >   0.236 </chord>
  <htailarea unit="M2">   0.063 </htailarea>
  <htailarm  unit="M" >   0.500 </htailarm>
  <vtailarea unit="M2">   0.034 </vtailarea>  <!-- twin fins, ENLARGED (was 0.0032) -->
  <vtailarm  unit="M" >   0.500 </vtailarm>
  <location name="AERORP" unit="M">   <!-- ref = wing aerodynamic centre -->
    <x> 0.0 </x> <y> 0.0 </y> <z> 0.0 </z>
  </location>
  <location name="EYEPOINT" unit="M">
    <x> -0.15 </x> <y> 0.0 </y> <z> -0.05 </z>
  </location>
  <location name="VRP" unit="M">
    <x> 0.0 </x> <y> 0.0 </y> <z> 0.0 </z>
  </location>
</metrics>

<mass_balance>
  <!-- 1.4 kg AUW; inertias are engineering estimates for a 1.3 m foam UAV -->
  <ixx unit="KG*M2">  0.045 </ixx>
  <iyy unit="KG*M2">  0.030 </iyy>
  <izz unit="KG*M2">  0.070 </izz>
  <emptywt unit="KG"> 1.10  </emptywt>   <!-- + 0.30 kg pack tank = 1.40 AUW -->
  <location name="CG" unit="M">
    <!-- 33% MAC aft of wing-LE-MAC; wing AC (ref) is at 25% MAC -->
    <x> 0.0189 </x> <y> 0.0 </y> <z> 0.0 </z>
  </location>
</mass_balance>

<ground_reactions>
  <!-- four VTOL landing legs in a rectangle straddling the CG (struct x ~ 0.02).
       Soft springs — this is a 1.4 kg foam UAV. Previous 3-point layout
       (single fwd point) tipped the model over on the ground. -->
  <contact type="BOGEY" name="LEG_FL">
    <location unit="M"> <x>-0.22</x> <y>-0.26</y> <z>-0.13</z> </location>
    <static_friction>0.9</static_friction><dynamic_friction>0.6</dynamic_friction>
    <rolling_friction>0.5</rolling_friction>
    <spring_coeff unit="N/M">700</spring_coeff>
    <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC">90</damping_coeff>
    <max_steer unit="DEG">0.0</max_steer><brake_group>NONE</brake_group><retractable>0</retractable>
  </contact>
  <contact type="BOGEY" name="LEG_FR">
    <location unit="M"> <x>-0.22</x> <y> 0.26</y> <z>-0.13</z> </location>
    <static_friction>0.9</static_friction><dynamic_friction>0.6</dynamic_friction>
    <rolling_friction>0.5</rolling_friction>
    <spring_coeff unit="N/M">700</spring_coeff>
    <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC">90</damping_coeff>
    <max_steer unit="DEG">0.0</max_steer><brake_group>NONE</brake_group><retractable>0</retractable>
  </contact>
  <contact type="BOGEY" name="LEG_RL">
    <location unit="M"> <x> 0.28</x> <y>-0.26</y> <z>-0.13</z> </location>
    <static_friction>0.9</static_friction><dynamic_friction>0.6</dynamic_friction>
    <rolling_friction>0.5</rolling_friction>
    <spring_coeff unit="N/M">700</spring_coeff>
    <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC">90</damping_coeff>
    <max_steer unit="DEG">0.0</max_steer><brake_group>NONE</brake_group><retractable>0</retractable>
  </contact>
  <contact type="BOGEY" name="LEG_RR">
    <location unit="M"> <x> 0.28</x> <y> 0.26</y> <z>-0.13</z> </location>
    <static_friction>0.9</static_friction><dynamic_friction>0.6</dynamic_friction>
    <rolling_friction>0.5</rolling_friction>
    <spring_coeff unit="N/M">700</spring_coeff>
    <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC">90</damping_coeff>
    <max_steer unit="DEG">0.0</max_steer><brake_group>NONE</brake_group><retractable>0</retractable>
  </contact>
</ground_reactions>

<propulsion>
  <!-- forward/cruise motor = the airframe's actual choice: A2212 2200KV + 1045.
       (The DJI E305/9450 stand-in undersized the static thrust and its 960 Kv
        motor sat at near-zero thrust across most of the throttle band at
        cruise speed — see aero/RESULTS.md propulsion note.) -->
  <engine file="A2212_2200KV">
    <location unit="M"> <x>0.20</x> <y>0.0</y> <z>0.0</z> </location>
    <orient unit="DEG"> <roll>0</roll><pitch>0</pitch><yaw>0</yaw> </orient>
    <feed>0</feed>
    <thruster file="APC_1045">
      <location unit="M"> <x>0.25</x> <y>0.0</y> <z>0.0</z> </location>
      <orient unit="DEG"> <roll>0</roll><pitch>0</pitch><yaw>0</yaw> </orient>
    </thruster>
  </engine>
  <tank type="FUEL" number="0">   <!-- stand-in for the LiPo pack -->
    <location unit="M"> <x>0.0</x> <y>0.0</y> <z>0.0</z> </location>
    <capacity unit="KG"> 0.30 </capacity>
    <contents unit="KG"> 0.30 </contents>
  </tank>
</propulsion>

<!-- ============================================================
     VTOL + forward thrust for the ArduPilot SITL bridge.
     The bridge (flight_software/jsbsim/jsbsim_bridge.py) sets each
     external_reactions/*/magnitude (in LBF) every frame from the PWM
     ArduPilot sends. The <propulsion> engine above is NOT started by the
     bridge — all thrust comes from here. Thrust models are SIMPLE
     (calibrated, not measured — see PROPULSION_NOTES.md): trust the
     fixed-wing cruise/aero, treat hover/transition thrust as indicative.
       location = structural frame (X aft+, Y right+, Z up+)
       direction = body frame (X fwd+, Y right+, Z down+)
     Lift-motor order follows ArduPilot quad-X: M1 FR, M2 RL, M3 FL, M4 RR.
     ============================================================ -->
<external_reactions>
  <force name="liftM1" frame="BODY">   <!-- front-right -->
    <location unit="M"><x>-0.13</x><y> 0.42</y><z>0.03</z></location>
    <direction><x>0</x><y>0</y><z>-1</z></direction>
  </force>
  <force name="liftM2" frame="BODY">   <!-- rear-left -->
    <location unit="M"><x> 0.17</x><y>-0.42</y><z>0.03</z></location>
    <direction><x>0</x><y>0</y><z>-1</z></direction>
  </force>
  <force name="liftM3" frame="BODY">   <!-- front-left -->
    <location unit="M"><x>-0.13</x><y>-0.42</y><z>0.03</z></location>
    <direction><x>0</x><y>0</y><z>-1</z></direction>
  </force>
  <force name="liftM4" frame="BODY">   <!-- rear-right -->
    <location unit="M"><x> 0.17</x><y> 0.42</y><z>0.03</z></location>
    <direction><x>0</x><y>0</y><z>-1</z></direction>
  </force>
  <force name="fwdMotor" frame="BODY">   <!-- rear pusher -->
    <location unit="M"><x>0.50</x><y>0</y><z>0.02</z></location>
    <direction><x>1</x><y>0</y><z>0</z></direction>
  </force>
  <!-- yaw-reaction couple: two opposed side forces fore/aft => pure M_z.
       bridge sets both magnitudes equal (may be negative). -->
  <force name="yawTorqueF" frame="BODY">
    <location unit="M"><x>-0.80</x><y>0</y><z>0</z></location>
    <direction><x>0</x><y>1</y><z>0</z></direction>
  </force>
  <force name="yawTorqueA" frame="BODY">
    <location unit="M"><x> 0.80</x><y>0</y><z>0</z></location>
    <direction><x>0</x><y>-1</y><z>0</z></direction>
  </force>
</external_reactions>

<flight_control name="FCS: CoconutQuadplane">
  <!-- real airframe uses 2 wing elevons; here elevator = symmetric elevon,
       aileron = differential elevon (JSBSim standard split). -->
  <channel name="Pitch">
    <aerosurface_scale name="Elevator Control">
      <input>fcs/elevator-cmd-norm</input>
      <range><min>-0.35</min><max>0.35</max></range>
      <output>fcs/elevator-pos-rad</output>
    </aerosurface_scale>
  </channel>
  <channel name="Roll">
    <aerosurface_scale name="Aileron Control">
      <input>fcs/aileron-cmd-norm</input>
      <range><min>-0.30</min><max>0.30</max></range>
      <output>fcs/aileron-pos-rad</output>
    </aerosurface_scale>
  </channel>
  <channel name="Yaw">
    <!-- no rudder on this airframe; channel kept zeroed for completeness -->
    <aerosurface_scale name="Rudder Control">
      <input>fcs/rudder-cmd-norm</input>
      <gain>0.0</gain>
      <range><min>-0.01</min><max>0.01</max></range>
      <output>fcs/rudder-pos-rad</output>
    </aerosurface_scale>
  </channel>
</flight_control>

<aerodynamics>

  <!-- alpha / beta limited to +-25 deg for the derivative terms. This model
       is a CRUISE fit (valid ~ -8..16 deg); during VTOL hover/transition the
       real AoA/sideslip briefly leave that range and a linear extrapolation
       would blow up. Clamping keeps the bridge stable; hover/transition aero
       is therefore only indicative. -->
  <function name="aero/alpha-rad-lim">
    <table>
      <independentVar>aero/alpha-rad</independentVar>
      <tableData>
        -3.15  -0.436
        -0.436 -0.436
         0.436  0.436
         3.15   0.436
      </tableData>
    </table>
  </function>
  <function name="aero/beta-rad-lim">
    <table>
      <independentVar>aero/beta-rad</independentVar>
      <tableData>
        -3.15  -0.436
        -0.436 -0.436
         0.436  0.436
         3.15   0.436
      </tableData>
    </table>
  </function>

  <!-- ================= LIFT ================= -->
  <axis name="LIFT">
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CL_alpha">
      <description>C_L vs alpha, whole aircraft (AeroBuildup, V=12 m/s),
                   wing incidence 1 deg baked in; stall knee tabulated</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <table>
          <independentVar>aero/alpha-deg</independentVar>
          <tableData>
            -8.0   -0.239
            -6.0   -0.055
            -4.0    0.128
            -2.0    0.310
             0.0    0.430
             2.0    0.612
             4.0    0.792
             6.0    0.968
             8.0    1.138
            10.0    1.261
            12.0    1.330
            14.0    1.301
            16.0    1.180
          </tableData>
        </table>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CLq">
      <description>Lift due to pitch rate</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>aero/ci2vel</property>
        <property>velocities/q-aero-rad_sec</property>
        <value> 4.52 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CLde">
      <description>Lift from symmetric elevon — large (full-span 28%c flap),
                   CL_de ~ 3.16 /rad (aero/control_authority.py)</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>fcs/elevator-pos-rad</property>
        <value> 3.16 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <!-- ================= DRAG ================= -->
  <axis name="DRAG">
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CD0">
      <description>Parasite drag (wing+tail+pod+booms buildup)</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <value> 0.0196 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CDi">
      <description>Induced drag, k = 1/(pi e AR), e ~ 0.79</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>aero/cl-squared</property>
        <value> 0.0713 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CDde">
      <description>Drag due to elevon deflection</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <abs><property>fcs/elevator-pos-rad</property></abs>
        <value> 0.10 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <!-- ================= SIDE ================= -->
  <axis name="SIDE">
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CYb">
      <description>Side force due to sideslip (enlarged twin fins)</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>aero/beta-rad-lim</property>
        <value> -0.242 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/CYr">
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
        <property>velocities/r-aero-rad_sec</property>
        <value> 0.15 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <!-- ================= PITCH ================ -->
  <axis name="PITCH">
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cm0">
      <description>Zero-alpha pitching moment</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
        <value> -0.068 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cmalpha">
      <description>Pitch stiffness about the wing-AC ref (CG offset via mass_balance)</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/alpha-rad-lim</property>
        <value> -1.671 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cmq">
      <description>Pitch damping</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/ci2vel</property>
        <property>velocities/q-aero-rad_sec</property>
        <value> -10.13 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cmde">
      <description>Pitch control power (symmetric elevon) — |Cm_de| = 0.38 /rad
                   about CG 33% MAC (aero/control_authority.py). Sign is JSBSim
                   convention (TE-down elevator -> nose down); confirm against
                   the ArduPilot elevon mixing at the SITL-bridge step.</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
        <property>fcs/elevator-pos-rad</property>
        <value> -0.38 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <!-- ================= ROLL ================= -->
  <axis name="ROLL">
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Clb">
      <description>Dihedral effect (assumes ~3 deg wing dihedral)</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/beta-rad-lim</property>
        <value> -0.040 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Clp">
      <description>Roll damping</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
        <property>velocities/p-aero-rad_sec</property>
        <value> -0.443 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Clr">
      <description>Roll due to yaw rate</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
        <property>velocities/r-aero-rad_sec</property>
        <value> 0.124 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Clda">
      <description>Roll control power (differential elevon) — |Cl_da| = 0.72 /rad
                   (full-span elevons, aero/control_authority.py). Roll authority
                   is very high (~650 deg/s at full throw); ArduPilot rate/expo
                   limiting expected. Confirm sign at the SITL-bridge step.</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>fcs/aileron-pos-rad</property>
        <value> 0.72 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <!-- ================= YAW ================== -->
  <axis name="YAW">
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cnb">
      <description>Weathercock stability — ENLARGED fins, target met (~0.071/rad)</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/beta-rad-lim</property>
        <value> 0.071 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cnr">
      <description>Yaw damping</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
        <property>velocities/r-aero-rad_sec</property>
        <value> -0.080 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cnp">
      <description>Yaw due to roll rate</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
        <property>velocities/p-aero-rad_sec</property>
        <value> -0.060 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/coefficient/Cnda">
      <description>Adverse yaw from differential elevon</description>
      <product>
        <property>aero/qbar-area</property>
        <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
        <property>fcs/aileron-pos-rad</property>
        <value> -0.006 </value>
      </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

</aerodynamics>

</fdm_config>
